n: 4.1.5
name: zig-and-hex
kind: hub
is: Zig 0.17.1 is pre-1.0 and its 0.17.0 release removed language features and changed one so that code can break without a compile error, while zig cc cross-compiles C for every target from a 51 MiB download. A hex or assembly seed is proven on Linux from 256 bytes; macOS supports no statically linked binaries, so a hex seed there would be a complete signed, dynamically linked Mach-O image.
at: 2026-11-24
by: r1/web-bootstrap-language

n: 4.1.5.1
name: zig-state
kind: observation
is: Zig's latest stable was 0.17.1 of 2026-11-02 (51 MiB, macOS aarch64). The 0.17.0 notes remove @cImport, four other features and two linkage kinds, and change @bitCast so code can break with no compile error; aarch64-macos is Tier 2, its self-hosted backend blocked on linker work. Zig builds for all its targets from any host; zig cc compiles C.
status: relayed
src: 2.11.41 2.11.42 2.11.43 2.11.1#346-355
limit: Zig is not installed on the study machine; nothing about it was run. The four features are array multiplication, void{}, the errdefer capture and i0; the linkage kinds are internal and link_once.
at: 2026-11-24
by: r1/web-bootstrap-language

